# L §6.1, §5.1 (pick P44; the builder's STOP-REPORT, R9's reach): every file's header states `tally N`, so a joint
# model file without it is refused by its own header check, LOAD-HEADER, before its members' versions are compared.
# refcore 2.1.7 compared them first and printed `LOAD-VERSION member a declares tally 2, the joint model None`.
=== joint.tally
model family
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "members/ana.tally" sha256 "da53b6ff6a096d47b9af5e16e8276735e72b3c343160d17d841c6ba432df1720"

ask r: a.rate
=== members/ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
input rate: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.12 "umowa"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-HEADER missing tally version (joint.tally:1)
